From bbbba139f51a3ee66db594f17f7ffb51d1d89fb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stel777 <274792865+Stel777@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 10:48:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] fix(ssd): reliable eject + asymptotic loading ring

db.rs: drop the 256 MiB mmap (PRAGMA mmap_size=0) before the WAL checkpoint on eject, so every SSD handle is freed without the app having to exit - releasing the mapping is what lets CM_Request_Device_Eject stop getting vetoed by a lingering section.

watcher + eject: stop the relaunch-and-re-lock loop. On a failed eject the helper drops a suppress sentinel so the re-armed watcher treats the already-present SSD as baseline instead of reopening the app (which re-grabbed the drive). A genuine unplug+replug still auto-opens.

splash: the fill ring is now asymptotic - it eases toward a cap and only completes when the app window actually appears, so a full ring always means the app is up (no more full-and-waiting).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
